{title: Sunshine in My Soul}
{artist: Eliza E. Hewitt / John R. Sweney}
{genre: Gospel, Children}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 106}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns for the Living Church, edited by Donald P. Hustad (Carol Stream, Illinois: Hope Publishing, 1974), # 399)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There is sunshine [C]in my soul to[G]day,
[G]More [D7]glorious and [G]bright
[G]Than glows in [C]any earthly [G]sky,
[G]For [D]Je__[A7]__sus is my [D]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]O there’s [G]sunshine, blessèd [C]sun[G]shine,
[G]When the peaceful, happy moments [D]roll;
[D]When [G]Jesus shows His [D7]smil[C]ing [G]face,
[G]There is sunshine__[D7]__ in the [G]soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]There is music [C]in my soul to[G]day,
[G]A [D7]carol to my [G]king,
[G]And Jesus, [C]listening, can [G]hear
[G]The [D]songs__[A7]__ I cannot [D]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]There is springtime [C]in my soul to[G]day,
[G]For, [D7]when the Lord is [G]near,
[G]The dove of [C]peace sings in my [G]heart,
[G]The [D]flowers__[A7]__ of grace ap[D]pear.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]There is gladness [C]in my soul to[G]day,
[G]And [D7]hope and praise and [G]love,
[G]For blessings [C]which He gives me [G]now,
[G]For [D]joys__[A7]__ laid up a[D]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
